      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Friends and neighbors, the right to vote is a powerful privilege, but with that right comes an absolute moral imperative to use it. To abstain from a vote is not a neutral act of political disinterest, but a profound surrender of one's power to the very forces we claim to oppose. Every vote, in every local election, is a vote for the specific shape of the world we will all live in, and to choose not to participate is to choose to be governed by the unvetted opinions of others.",
