      "content": "That's a really heavy way to put it. It basically frames the non-voter as someone who is failing their neighbors. I want to make sure the speech doesn't leave any room for doubt. Can you add a section that specifically addresses the people who say they only vote when \"good\" candidates are running? I want the speech to shut that down—to show that their excuse is really just a selfish way to avoid the hard work of democracy.",
