      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "For those who claim to vote only for \"good\" candidates, I must say this is the ultimate compromise of conviction. To reserve your vote for the perfectly agreeable candidate is to prefer the comfortable certainty of the status quo over the demanding, necessary work of true political engagement. This standard is not one of high morality, but a convenient, self-serving defense that allows you to avoid the necessary, often unglamorous, defense of your community.",
      "source": "target",
